# Fish Audio Python SDK scoped source review

Reviewed: 2026-10-25. Source: [fishaudio/fish-audio-python](https://github.com/fishaudio/fish-audio-python), commit [448150989781e6f91c3ca9f6cc59711a87df8130](https://github.com/fishaudio/fish-audio-python/commit/448150989781e6f91c3ca9f6cc59711a87df8130), committed 2026-07-31. Scope: TTS types and playback helper only; no SDK installation or network calls. Related: [media processing](../media-processing.md), [Fish service review](external--fish-speech.md), [channel input](../channel-input.md).

The [reference type](https://github.com/fishaudio/fish-audio-python/blob/448150989781e6f91c3ca9f6cc59711a87df8130/src/fishaudio/types/tts.py#L10-L19) carries audio bytes and matching text, supporting the distinction between persistent voice IDs and per-request conditioning. [Configuration fields](https://github.com/fishaudio/fish-audio-python/blob/448150989781e6f91c3ca9f6cc59711a87df8130/src/fishaudio/types/tts.py#L55-L110) include codec, sample rate, chunking and sampling controls. These are useful semantic inputs, but an SDK default is not proof of the current hosted API default or effect. The inspected types do not state PCM byte order.

The [stream helper](https://github.com/fishaudio/fish-audio-python/blob/448150989781e6f91c3ca9f6cc59711a87df8130/src/fishaudio/utils/stream.py#L9-L79) checks `mpv` using `which`, starts playback, writes every incoming chunk and accumulates a complete byte buffer. Cleanup closes stdin and waits for the player. This is a convenient sample, not the harness's bounded playback design: there is no explicit output cap, time budget or cancellation acknowledgment in this function, and `which` is not a portable Windows executable-discovery contract.

Adoption: use the request types as reference evidence while retaining the harness's own subprocess and artifact boundaries. A future live playback adapter should own a bounded queue, backpressure, device cancellation and partial-output state, without forcing every stream into memory. Prefer inspectable WAV/MP3 output until the hosted raw-PCM interpretation is independently established. Neither successful type construction nor an audio iterator proves that playback, cancellation or model inference worked on the target device.
